      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "INCENTIVISE NZ (8) is newcomer to the Bailey McDonough yard from NZ where he has put together a string of wins and placings, scoring a resuming win when last seen at Alexandra Park last month. Draws wide but won his lone try at this distance and should measure up. SUSPICIOUS CAPTAIN NZ (5) is another former Kiwi who comes off a dominant win at his Australian debut, cruising home by 12m at Wagga. Hart goes on and he has plenty of upside. IRON MIKE TYSON NZ (7) came from this barrier to kick off for Brad Hewitt with a 1.7m win at Bathurst. That was his first hitout for five months so he should be improved. COHEN THE RED (1) was fourth from this barrier to star colt Loucasso when last seen in the Breeders Challenge Final. The ace draw should see him competitive again. A SPECIAL OCCASION NZ (6) tackles a stronger bunch but is progressing well, coming from wider barriers to record two wins and a second from his last three outings at this circuit and distance.",
